From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:19:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Desktop readers find the CLI config where the CLI does

Skills, subagents, commands, hooks, MCP sync, plugin sync, settings sync and
the CUA check each built ~/.zcode/cli from their own home lookup, so in an
isolated profile they read a different file than the CLI wrote (an installed
skill plugin counted as disabled). One helper resolves it: ZCODE_HOME, then
the desktop home, then HOME. Production paths are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
